--- !u!114 &1060543985
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1060543983}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "In this world, you can change the parameters of SaccFlightAndVehicles
    and check the movement of the aircraft.\nHowever, there are some elements that
    cannot be changed in this world.\r\nAlso, the movement of the aircraft is affected
    by the shape(collider) of the aircraft.\r\nTherefore, even if the parameters
    are the same, the movements will differ depending on the aircraft.\nExample value
    settings and the world itself are available at https://github.com/shinchan-dot/AircraftInspector.\n\r\r\n\r\nTips
    for modifying basic flight characteristics of aircraft: (From Instructions.txt
    of SaccFlightAndVehicles)\r\nIf it's having trouble taking off, try adjusting
    the center of mass and pitch moment positions, as well as the ground effect settings.\r\nThe
    Strength and Friction values for pitch, yaw, and roll are important, and both
    play off each other. You may need to set them to very high values, especially
    if you make a large plane.\r\nRot Multi Max Speed will need to be adjusted for
    planes with different speeds. It's the speed at which (in meters per second)
    the plane reaches maximum responsiveness.\r\nVel Straighten Str Pitch/Yaw are
    Very important to the handling of the plane. They push the nose toward the velocity
    direction. (they also interact with pitch and yaw strength)\r\nLift and Max Lift
    are also very important, and a bit tricky to tweak. If max lift is too high you
    can end up with a plane that can fly in circles extremely quickly. Reducing Max
    Lift will make the plane bleed much more speed in turns which is more realistic.
    Try around 3.\r\nThe Vel Lift/Max values are used to prevent the plane's nose
    from dropping constantly (counter gravity). Find a Vel Lift Max value that keeps
    the nose steady, Max is 10 by default but technically should be 9.81 to counter
    gravity exactly\r\nVel Lift value is used to decide how quickly the plane reaches
    Vel Lift Max.\r\nDon't change the angular drag or drag of the rigidbody, drag
    is handled by the script, and angular drag is set by the script as a workaround
    for a sync issue.\r\n\r\nIf you use the 'Auto Adjust Values To Mass' option,
    you can set the rigidbody mass to any value you wish with no effect on the performance
    of the vehicle.\r\nUsing this option you will notice a lot of the SaccAirVehicle's
    values change when entering play mode. If you wish to tweak values during play
    mode, set the rigidbody mass to 1 temporarily so that they don't change.\r\n\r\nTips
    for VTOL Only aircraft:\r\nFor helicopters, keep the VTOL Thrust Vec values at
    1, and adjust Pitch Yaw and Roll Strength\r\nPitch Down Lift Multi has a pretty
    big effect on how fast the vehicle can move forwards\r\nThe constant friction
    values are intended for helicopters (gyroscopic forces stop rotation)\r\nYou
    can make the blade tilt angle larger than implied in order to make the vehicle
    faster\r\nSet Adverse yaw to 0 if you don't want the helicopter to spin when
    increasing the throttle\r\nthe Vel Straighten values are just as important for
    the handling of helicopters as planes\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e2e8cd714049be242b67bc7c97be231e, type: 2}
